igured with node1 as writable primary and node2/node3 as standbys, with data replicating\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 initialized as primary with wal_level=replica, replication role, and physical slots; node2/node3 built via pg_basebackup -R and started as standbys. Inserted rows on node1 (baseline-row-1/2) confirmed present on both standbys with pg_is_in_recovery()=t.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c2168a052d374bc3\",\"cmd-47f6939f78314e6d\",\"cmd-a0a8389cf97a4690\",\"cmd-da3317a5d0a54b80\",\"cmd-634291d9ac3b4ba5\",\"cmd-7d31a97880434700\",\"cmd-2a4ddebb918643ee\",\"cmd-e3854a964fb94d6f\",\"cmd-22ce235eb589463c\"]},{\"id\":\"failover-promotion\",\"requirement\":\"When primary is lost, a standby takes over as writable primary without losing committed data\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Final row committed on node1 (LSN 0/40645B8) confirmed replayed by both standbys (0/40645F0) before node1's postgresql service was stopped, simulating primary loss. node2 promoted via pg_promote() (pg_is_in_recovery=f), all 3 pre-failover rows intact, and a new write succeeded, proving both no data loss and restored write availability.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d08f84f8ae5f417f\",\"cmd-8623f7a8bf7343a2\",\"cmd-1e35bf9995d64621\",\"cmd-2f7fce7c9cc94741\",\"cmd-522abbf2775e47de\"]},{\"id\":\"surviving-standby-repoint\",\"requirement\":\"Surviving standby (node3) re-pointed to stream from the newly promoted primary and kept in sync\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3 reconfigured with primary_conninfo pointing to node2; logs show timeline switch 1->2 and resumed streaming; node3 query shows all 4 rows including the post-failover insert; node2's pg_stat_replication confirms node3 streaming.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8ecc7c410a7d42e0\",\"cmd-5da03302bde447d5\",\"cmd-7b32e1667aab4728\"]},{\"id\":\"former-primary-rejoins\",\"requirement\":\"Recovered former primary (node1) comes back as a standby of whichever system is primary (node2), without data loss\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 restarted with standby.signal and primary_conninfo pointing to node2; logs show adoption of timeline 2; node1 query shows all 4 rows present; node2's pg_stat_replication lists both node1 and node3 streaming.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-cedfcd1cfe2b49d8\",\"cmd-d67a2af5ad4e4199\",\"cmd-be767de43b434666\"]},{\"id\":\"post-recovery-steady-state\",\"requirement\":\"Post-recovery cluster remains a healthy 3-node replication topology with fresh writes propagating\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A new row inserted on node2 (primary) appeared as count=5 on both node1 and node3, confirming steady-state replication after the full failover/recovery cycle.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b770b2b3f2f7442f\",\"cmd-e85c7007257d4b3c\",\"cmd-d7ce66ab987b4b33\"]},{\"id\":\"node-restart-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node: pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot IDs and health captured for all three nodes (bccb87ac/06339ff3/d052eb57). Each node rebooted one at a time (standbys first, node2/primary last) with acknowledgement returned pre-disconnect, unreachable/reachable transition observed, and boot_id confirmed changed post-restart (c5eae19e, 888e9aaf, 130d3c6e), matching the after_executor global snapshot. Service, replication role, and row counts (5/5, then 6/6 after final write) recovered on each node, with the standbys remaining up during the primary's restart (quorum preserved).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-52a79ec2c8bb4d1f\",\"cmd-a18a767b814b4659\",\"cmd-eebd6e1860714f2e\",\"cmd-3f4d8976dca544e9\",\"cmd-9390a3a98aea4857\",\"cmd-0c2040008b6d484f\",\"cmd-1ef084ed0c044b0b\",\"cmd-8728592efa1e468c\",\"cmd-4a880a3e4fc64e2c\",\"cmd-eed4b82c40da4c2c\",\"cmd-e6104173ebbc4cfa\",\"cmd-06f334f6f43c4f32\",\"cmd-dbc7c49428db41ed\",\"cmd-1f1524a0dca14b81\"