ss-checked against the fixed after_executor snapshot. No unnecessary or unreverted mutations were identified; the handful of failed commands were normal troubleshooting quickly corrected.\",\"limitations\":[\"Evidence relies on the executor's own captured command outputs rather than independent verification tooling, though outputs are direct psql/systemctl/log output rather than executor narrative.\",\"The two-node availability during node2's restart (quorum) is inferred from pg_stat_replication showing node1/node3 reconnect quickly, not from a continuous liveness probe during the exact restart window.\",\"Long-term persistence of postgresql.auto.conf settings across further reboots beyond the single verified cycle per node was not separately tested.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"initial-topology","requirement":"PostgreSQL streaming replication configured with node1 as writable primary and node2/node3 as standbys, with data replicating","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 initialized as primary with wal_level=replica, replication role, and physical slots; node2/node3 built via pg_basebackup -R and started as standbys. Inserted rows on node1 (baseline-row-1/2) confirmed present on both standbys with pg_is_in_recovery()=t.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c2168a052d374bc3","cmd-47f6939f78314e6d","cmd-a0a8389cf97a4690","cmd-da3317a5d0a54b80","cmd-634291d9ac3b4ba5","cmd-7d31a97880434700","cmd-2a4ddebb918643ee","cmd-e3854a964fb94d6f","cmd-22ce235eb589463c"]},{"id":"failover-promotion","requirement":"When primary is lost, a standby takes over as writable primary without losing committed data","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final row committed on node1 (LSN 0/40645B8) confirmed replayed by both standbys (0/40645F0) before node1's postgresql service was stopped, simulating primary loss. node2 promoted via pg_promote() (pg_is_in_recovery=f), all 3 pre-failover rows intact, and a new write succeeded, proving both no data loss and restored write availability.","evid